<title>UK: ICI sees German chemical output best in 1997.</title>
<headline>ICI sees German chemical output best in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>- Germany is expected see the largest rise in chemical output among major European producers in 1997, ICI Plc chief economist Richard Freeman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The following are the country forecasts for chemical output in volume terms from the UK Chemical Industries Association's economics appraisal committe, with comparitive percentage change figures for 1996.</p>
<p>			     1996	  1997</p>
<p>     Germany	    -0.6	  4.0</p>
<p>     France		2.8	  3.0</p>
<p>     Italy		 1.3	  3.5</p>
<p>     Britain	     2.1	  2.9</p>
<p>     Netherlands	 0.2	  3.6</p>
<p>     Spain		-0.4	  1.8</p>
<p>     Belgium	     1.9	  3.5</p>
<p>     Western Europe    1.0	  3.3</p>
<p>--London newsroom 44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
